# ============================================================================
# LOGINS — copy this file to ".env" and fill in the real usernames/passwords.
#   cp .env.example .env
# The ".env" file is PRIVATE. It is git-ignored and can never be committed.
# NEVER put real passwords in THIS file (.env.example is committed/shared).
#
# Easiest path: skip this file entirely and add logins in the app
# (Settings -> Roles & logins). There you create a role, tick which sites it
# applies to, and type a login per site — the app writes the right variables
# into your private .env for you. Role NAMES and which sites they apply to are
# saved in config/roles.json; only the USERNAMES/PASSWORDS land here in .env.
# ============================================================================
#
# Naming (most specific wins):
#   <ENV>_<ROLE>_USERNAME / <ENV>_<ROLE>_PASSWORD   per-environment login
#   <ROLE>_USERNAME       / <ROLE>_PASSWORD         shared across environments
#
#   ENV  = the environment name, uppercased, dashes -> underscores (staging -> STAGING)
#   ROLE = the name you pass to login(page, 'admin')  -> ADMIN
#
# The per-environment var (<ENV>_<ROLE>_*) wins; the shared <ROLE>_* is the
# fallback. If the same account works everywhere, set only the shared vars once.
# Only fill in the ones you actually use. Delete or add roles as needed.
#
# ---- 'example' role — NO SETUP NEEDED --------------------------------------
# The built-in `example` role (used by the committed @example tests against
# saucedemo) is pre-filled with saucedemo's PUBLIC demo credentials
# (standard_user / secret_sauce) as a built-in fallback. Leave it blank here —
# the example tests run zero-config on a fresh clone. Only add EXAMPLE_USERNAME /
# EXAMPLE_PASSWORD if you want to override those public creds.

# ---- shared across all environments (used when no env-specific var is set) --
ADMIN_USERNAME=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---- staging ---------------------------------------------------------------
STAGING_ADMIN_USERNAME=
STAGING_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---- production ------------------------------------------------------------
PRODUCTION_ADMIN_USERNAME=
PRODUCTION_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---- demo-dev ----
DEMO_DEV_ADMIN_USERNAME=
DEMO_DEV_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---- demo-stage ----
DEMO_STAGE_ADMIN_USERNAME=
DEMO_STAGE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
